cartograph/data/lafayette-square/*
!cartograph/data/lafayette-square/neighborhood_boundary.json
!cartograph/data/lafayette-square/geography.json
!cartograph/data/lafayette-square/buildings.json
# LS's hand-tuned species routing (park species name → roster id). Authored, not
# a reproducible fetch, so it stays tracked (unlike scripts/15's derived rewrite).
!cartograph/data/lafayette-square/tree-species-map.json
!cartograph/data/lafayette-square/raw/
!cartograph/data/lafayette-square/clean/
cartograph/data/lafayette-square/raw/*
!cartograph/data/lafayette-square/raw/osm.json
!cartograph/data/lafayette-square/raw/survey.json
!cartograph/data/lafayette-square/raw/elevation.json
!cartograph/data/lafayette-square/raw/osm_street_lamps.json
cartograph/data/lafayette-square/clean/*
!cartograph/data/lafayette-square/clean/map.json
!cartograph/data/lafayette-square/clean/park-polygon.json
# The authored PARK CENSUS well — City Forestry clipped to the park polygon, the
# hand-curated gem (source:'park'). Authored source (its raw maps6 export is NOT
# committed), so unlike the fetched clean/* wells it must stay tracked. Kept as an
# authored reference; the whole-hood City inventory (park_trees.json) subsumes it
# (750/756 overlap), so LS bakes City + OSM, not this.
!cartograph/data/lafayette-square/clean/park_census.json
# The REAL LS census wells that the slab is baked from. TRACKED (not the usual
# gitignored-clean/ treatment) so the recovered census can't be lost on a clean
# checkout or drift on re-fetch — the fix for the 756-vs-6,866 regression
# (scratch/CENSUS-RECOVERY-FINDINGS.md). Re-fetchable via scripts/13 (City maps9)
# + scripts/14 (OSM Overpass), but frozen here so the committed bake is reproducible.
!cartograph/data/lafayette-square/clean/park_trees.json
!cartograph/data/lafayette-square/clean/osm_trees.json
# ⭐⭐ THE GEOMETRY INPUTS — same rule as the census wells above, learned the same
# way. map.json and src/data/ribbons.json were tracked while the inputs that
# PRODUCE them were ignored, so "unchanged inputs" was never verifiable from git
# and the producing state was unrecoverable rather than merely unknown — that is
# the root of ROADMAP A01 (the pipeline does not reproduce its own committed
# output; measured by Tally 2026-07-31). overlay.json is AUTHORED: it carries the
# operator's measured street widths, and a reset on 2026-07-23 dropped it from 22
# streets-with-measure to 0 while the only surviving copies sat untracked, one
# `git clean` from gone. Frozen here so the committed bake is reproducible.
!cartograph/data/lafayette-square/clean/overlay.json
!cartograph/data/lafayette-square/clean/overlay.json.pre-reset
!cartograph/data/lafayette-square/clean/overlay.json.backup-*
!cartograph/data/lafayette-square/clean/skeleton.json
cartograph/node_modules/

# Claude Code local settings
.claude/

# ribbons.json snapshot backups created by the pipeline scripts.
# Useful locally for rollback; never wanted in source control.
src/data/ribbons.json.backup-*

# FOR-species20K LiDAR dataset (~51 GB, used as input to the Arborist
# tree-baking pipeline). Lives locally; never committed.
# Source: https://zenodo.org/records/13255198
botanica/

# Arborist operator state + caches. Curated picks live in arborist/state/;
# .laz → .ply preview conversion cache lives in arborist/_cache/. Both
# regenerable; never committed.
arborist/state/
# EXCEPT the hand-encoded species priors files — load-bearing artifacts
# per Project: Li'l Vera Cycle 1 rev. 2 (2026-05-20). Future species
# onboarding follows the same hand-encode → run → refine cycle.
!arborist/state/
!arborist/state/*/
arborist/state/*/*
!arborist/state/*/botanical-priors.json
arborist/_cache/
arborist/.venv/

# Arborist raw-GLB library. Authoring-only source pool the Arborist
# reads from; never read by runtime. The published artifact runtime
# consumes is the per-Look bake at public/baked/<look>/, written by
# arborist/bake-look.js. Library is multi-GB and regenerable; never
# commit it. See ARCHITECTURE.md §1 for the publish-loop rule.
public/trees/

# Atlas QA visualisations. `bake-look.js:658` writes one per atlas so you can
# eyeball the packing; NOTHING loads them at runtime (verified 2026-07-21 — no
# fetch/src/url reference anywhere in src/). They were tracked by accident and
# cost 20 MB of the ~1 GB GitHub-Pages payload. Regenerated by every bake, so
# they stay available locally — they just don't ship.
public/baked/*/trees-atlas-*-viz.png

# Local handoff/brief dispatch archive — kept on disk, out of git (Jacob, 2026-07-21)
_handoffs/

# D2 gate working artifacts (agent Plumb, 2026-08-08). `.d2-before.json` is the
# captured corner baseline (~1.4 MB) and `.d2-mutants/` holds generated COPIES of
# tileGround.mjs (~245 KB each) that the self-test builds and replays. Both are
# derivatives the tool regenerates on demand — the checker itself is tracked, its
# scratchpad is not. Dot-prefixed by the agent for exactly this reason.
scratch/.d2-*.json
scratch/.d2-mutants/
# The instrumented COPIES of tileGround.js that `claims-band-reaches-lu.mjs`
# builds (it now owns the loader `.d2-mutants/` used to hold). Same reasoning.
scratch/.band-probe/
# A10-③ (the iA source-edge stamp, 2026-08-09). Same rule, same reasoning: the
# checkers are tracked, their scratchpads are not.
# ⛔ `scratch/.iastamp-artifact.json` is deliberately NOT listed. It is COMMITTED,
# and that is right: at 396 bytes it survives a fresh clone, which is exactly what
# `ROADMAP` A10 complains that `a10-post-rim` does not do ("the baseline is not in
# git… regenerate it BEFORE you touch the cure"). A rule here would also be dead —
# gitignore never applies to a tracked file.
# ⚠️ But `claims-ia-source-stamp.mjs` PRINTS "…, gitignored" for it, which is false
# twice over. Fix the message, not the tracking.
scratch/.stamp-probe/
scratch/.fold-probe/
scratch/.mint-flip-*.json
scratch/.leg-probe/
scratch/.prov-probe/
scratch/.rekey-probe/
scratch/.notch-probe/
scratch/.rev-probe/
scratch/.lab-probe/
scratch/.arc-probe/
scratch/.ramp-probe/
scratch/_snapshots/
